// P3D.4 (IR6.1–IR6.17): the Inspection and Repair exercise on the Conrod stand-in
// (`fixtures/conrod_standin.cadrs`, inch, Steel; shipped broken with its history,
// `fixtures/conrod_standin.history.ron`). Its fillet is "Fillet 1" (the course's Fillet 4).
// 01 IR6.1: opened: Sketch 2 (unsolvable, open), Extrude 4 (its region gone) and Circular
//    pattern 1 (its seed failed) red; the header's "!".
// 02 IR6.2: Sketch 2 edited: "Sketch could not be solved."; the rod rolled back to it (every
//    feature after it grey and italic, their icons faded).
// 03 IR6.3–IR6.4: Constraint manager, Status → Errors: Equal 1 and both Ø dimensions red;
//    "Sort by" with its Constraint / Entity tabs inside the panel.
// 04 IR6.5: Equal 1 deleted with its trash; the rest solve.
// 05 IR6.6–IR6.7: Profile inspector: "Loose end" (the spur) and "Loose ends (2)" (bold,
//    selected), zoomed to the 0.02 in gap at the notch's apex; large red bubbles on the ends.
// 06 IR6.8: Coincident (I) on the two ends: the notch closes, its row goes.
// 07 accepted: no errors; the three notches are cut round the small end.
// 08 IR6.9: Sketch 3 edited, Ctrl+A, Delete: the slot gone; the web's face region is left.
// 09 IR6.10: Offset (O), a click in the web's face region, a click 0.1 in inside, 0.1 in
//    typed: the face's outer loop (used from the kernel's edges, construction, dash-dot) and
//    its offset, with the 0.1 dimension.
// 10 the new region selected: "Area: 2.279 in²" at the bottom right.
// 11 accepted: Extrude 5 (its region gone) and Fillet 1 (its edge gone) red.
// 12 IR6.11: History, its Repair icon (pressed; the blue banner), "2 changes" (mine) opened:
//    "Conrod :: Edit : Sketch 3", "Conrod :: Edit : Sketch 2"; the stand-in author's "13
//    changes" closed; Start.
// 13 IR6.12: "Conrod :: Edit : Sketch 2" picked, History closed: the Repair panel beside the
//    viewport shows that state (the slot pocket), "Viewing Main :: Conrod :: Edit : Sketch 2",
//    its own view cube, Synchronize view on; both halves fitted; the Repair icon (wrench) in
//    the right strip.
// 14 IR6.13: Extrude 5 edited, the pointer on "Missing Face of Sketch 3" (the whole label):
//    the slot's outline lights up yellow in the Repair panel; the Replace reference icon shows
//    over the item's right end.
// 14b the pointer on the icon: its "Replace reference" tooltip.
// 15 IR6.14: Replace reference beside the dialog: Selection to replace (red), Selection to
//    replace with (active), Propagate changes; the new region picked (Sketch 3 is shown while
//    Extrude 5 is edited): "Face of Sketch 3", Extrude 5 previews the trapezoid pocket.
// 16 ✓ on Extrude 5 accepts both dialogs: only Fillet 1 is red; Sketch 3, now used, hidden.
// 16b IR6.14: Sketch 3 shown with its eye (the offset over the new pocket), then hidden again
//    (Sketch 3 shows by itself while Extrude 5 is edited, so the eye comes after the ✓ here).
// 17 IR6.15: Fillet 1 edited, the pointer on "Missing Edge of Extrude 5": the slot's floor (the
//    edge's tangent chain, 4 edges) lights up in the Repair panel.
// 18 IR4.7: Replace reference with one floor edge of the new pocket: its corners aren't
//    tangent, so it stands for 1 of the 4 edges; the note says so.
// 19 IR6.16: the pocket's floor face instead: "Face of Extrude 5", the note gone.
// 20 accepted: no errors remain.
// 21 IR6.17: Repair closed (the view full width again), Conrod's Mass properties: 0.530 lb,
//    1.868 in³ (the healthy model's).
Scenario(
    start: Some("document"),
    steps: [
        WaitFor("document-shell"),
        Custom("fixture conrod_standin"),
        Key("P"),
        Key("Shift+7"),
        Key("F"),
        MoveTo(1420, 900),
        Wait(3),
